# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hindsight stack configuration. Copy to .env and edit:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit it -- it holds your database password and,
# depending on the provider you pick, an LLM credential.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. PostgreSQL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required. Any non-empty string; it is only used between the two containers.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 24
HINDSIGHT_DB_PASSWORD=

# Optional, defaults shown.
# HINDSIGHT_DB_USER=hindsight_user
# HINDSIGHT_DB_NAME=hindsight_db

# The Postgres image. The default is a ghcr.io image, NOT upstream's
# pgvector/pgvector, because Docker Hub is blocked on the network this was built
# on (403 through the host proxy). See docs/REGISTRY.md for what was tested. If
# Docker Hub is reachable for you, pgvector/pgvector works too.
#
# Any replacement must: use the official postgres entrypoint, ship the `vector`
# and `pg_trgm` extensions, honor PGDATA, and be PostgreSQL 14+.
# HINDSIGHT_DB_IMAGE=ghcr.io/tensorchord/vchord-postgres:pg17-v0.4.3

# Changing the Postgres major version will NOT migrate an existing volume.
# Postgres refuses to open a data directory written by a different major version.
# To move versions, dump and restore.

# Which vector extension Hindsight should use. The default image ships both
# `pgvector` and `vchord`; pgvector is Hindsight's default and best-tested path.
# HINDSIGHT_API_VECTOR_EXTENSION=pgvector


# ── 2. LLM provider ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required. Hindsight calls an LLM for fact extraction, entity resolution and
# answer generation. Embeddings and reranking do NOT come from here -- the full
# image runs those locally in-container.
#
# Upstream supports: openai, openai-responses, groq, ollama, gemini, anthropic,
# lmstudio, vertexai, minimax, deepseek, zai, atlas, volcano, openai-codex,
# claude-code, github-copilot

# ── 2a. A provider with a plain API key (simplest path) ──────────────────────
# Uncomment one. Nothing else to run.
#
# OpenAI:
HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY=sk-xxx
HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# Anthropic direct:
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxx
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
#
# Groq:
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=groq
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY=gsk_xxx
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ── 2b. A provider whose credential expires ──────────────────────────────────
# Skip this block unless your provider is fronted by an OIDC broker, an SSO
# gateway or an STS, so the credential is a bearer that expires in minutes to an
# hour rather than a long-lived key.
#
# Hindsight reads its API key from config once and has no refresh hook, so a
# short-lived bearer works until it expires and then 401s forever.
# scripts/token-shim.py is the fix: a loopback proxy that holds a live bearer,
# refreshing 5 minutes before expiry, and swaps it in. It is the equivalent of
# Claude Code's apiKeyHelper for a tool that has no such hook.
#
# Comment out 2a, uncomment this, and start it with `make shim` before `make up`.
# Read docs/TOKEN-SHIM.md first.
#
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# Any non-empty placeholder. The shim replaces it with the real bearer, but
# Hindsight refuses to start on an empty key.
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_API_KEY=via-shim
# The shim, as seen from inside the container -- NOT 127.0.0.1, which inside a
# container is the container. `make preflight` verifies it is actually reachable.
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8787/v1
# HINDSIGHT_API_LLM_MODEL=your-model-id
#
# Port the shim binds on the host. Must match the base URL above.
# SHIM_PORT=8787
# Where the shim forwards to, and the command that prints a bearer to stdout.
# SHIM_UPSTREAM=https://api.example.com
# SHIM_TOKEN_CMD=/path/to/your-token-command
# Refresh this many seconds before the token's `exp`. With a 60-minute token,
# 300 means the helper runs about every 55 minutes.
# SHIM_REFRESH_MARGIN=300
#
# OPTIONAL. A second credential some gateways want alongside the bearer.
# SHIM_EXTRA_HEADER=X-Project-Token
# SHIM_EXTRA_HEADER_VALUE=
#
# OPTIONAL. Literal values your token helper prints when it is NOT returning a
# bearer. Listed here, they fail loudly at startup instead of as an opaque
# upstream 401. See docs/TOKEN-SHIM.md section 6.
# SHIM_REJECT_TOKENS=
#
# OPTIONAL. Run a local, gitignored shim instead of the generic one, for a
# provider you would rather not describe in a public repo. Section 8 of
# docs/TOKEN-SHIM.md.
# SHIM_SCRIPT=scripts/my-provider-shim.py


# ── 3. Ports on the host ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both bind to 127.0.0.1 only. Change these if something already holds the port.
# HINDSIGHT_API_PORT=8888
# HINDSIGHT_CP_PORT=9999


# ── 4. Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin the image instead of tracking :latest. Recommended once it works, so a
# `docker compose pull` cannot change the version under you.
# HINDSIGHT_VERSION=latest

# Stable worker identity. Keep it stable across restarts or tasks interrupted by
# a restart are orphaned under the old ID.
# HINDSIGHT_API_WORKER_ID=hindsight-local

# Shared secret required to log in to the Control Plane web UI. Empty means the
# UI is open to anyone who can reach 127.0.0.1:9999.
# HINDSIGHT_CP_ACCESS_KEY=

# ── 5. API authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hindsight ships with NO authentication. This enables the built-in API-key
# extension, which gates EVERY endpoint including /mcp. One key covers both,
# because ApiKeyTenantExtension.authenticate_mcp() delegates to authenticate().
#
# Clients send:  Authorization: Bearer <key>
# Generate one:  openssl rand -hex 32
# Rotate:        change the value, then `make restart`, then update every client.
#
# Required whenever the API is reachable beyond loopback -- `make serve-on`
# publishes it to your tailnet, and MCP exposes retain/delete/clear.
HINDSIGHT_API_TENANT_EXTENSION=hindsight_api.extensions.builtin.tenant:ApiKeyTenantExtension
HINDSIGHT_API_TENANT_API_KEY=
